### Identity Broker helper requests
### Use this file to register an IntelliJ HTTP Client OAuth client for
### `money-mate-api-token-exchange/money-mate-api.http`.
###
### Recommended flow:
### 1. Run the metadata request to confirm the broker is up.
### 2. Run the DCR request.
### 3. Copy the returned `client_id` into:
###    money-mate-api-token-exchange/http-client.env.json

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9000
@redirectUri = http://127.0.0.1:63342/api/http-client/oauth2/callback
@clientName = money-mate-api-token-exchange-intellij

### Authorization Server Metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

### Dynamic Client Registration for IntelliJ HTTP Client
# @name registerIntellijClient
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth2/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_name": "{{clientName}}",
  "redirect_uris": [
    "{{redirectUri}}"
  ],
  "grant_types": [
    "authorization_code",
    "refresh_token"
  ],
  "response_types": [
    "code"
  ],
  "token_endpoint_auth_method": "none",
  "scope": "openid profile hypermedia.access"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("tokenExchangeHttpClientId", response.body.client_id);
  client.log("Registered client_id: " + response.body.client_id);
%}

